<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hosseinqoli Khan Bakhtiari</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1882">1882</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Hosseinqoli Khan Ilkhani</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hosseinqoli Khan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bakhtiari">Bakhtiari</a> was a chief of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haft-lang">Haft Lang</a> Bakhtiari who united the confederation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagros-mountains">Zagros</a> under his leadership. In 1867 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qajar-dynasty">Qajar</a> government recognised him as ilkhan, paramount chief, of all the Bakhtiari. His growing power alarmed the Qajar governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zell-e-soltan">Zell-e Soltan</a>, who had him killed in 1882; his sons led the Bakhtiari in the Constitutional Revolution.</p></div>
